  "title": "T-plurals that use KPT",
  "summary": "Change the consonant stem first and add plural -t second.",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the KPT change in a plural.",
    "Build the weak noun stem.",
    "Add -t only after the stem is ready."
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Two construction steps",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Many nouns use the weak KPT grade before nominative plural -t. First build the weak stem; then add the plural ending.",
        "Keeping the steps separate makes the form easier to understand: noun → weak stem → plural."
      ],
      "keyPoints": ["pankki → panki- → pankit", "pelto → pello- → pellot"]
    },
    {
      "title": "The same familiar KPT pairs",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Double consonants can shorten, a single p can become v, and consonant clusters can change. The worked forms below show the weak stem for each supplied noun; learn that stem before adding -t.",
        "The final -t is the plural ending. A t created inside the stem is not the plural ending."
      ],
      "keyPoints": ["kk → k", "p → v", "lt → ll"]
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "finnish": "pankki → pankit",
      "english": "bank → banks",
      "steps": [
        "Use the known change kk → k: pankki → panki-.",
        "Add the known plural ending -t: pankit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "kauppa → kaupat",
      "english": "shop → shops",
      "steps": [
        "Use the known change pp → p: kauppa → kaupa-.",
        "Add the known plural ending -t: kaupat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "keitto → keitot",
      "english": "soup → soups",
      "steps": [
        "keitto (“soup”) is supplied as context.",
        "tt → t gives the weak stem keito-.",
        "Add plural -t: keitot (“soups”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "silta → sillat",
      "english": "bridge → bridges",
      "steps": [
        "silta (“bridge”) is supplied as context.",
        "lt → ll gives the weak stem silla-.",
        "Add plural -t: sillat (“bridges”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "kampa → kammat",
      "english": "comb → combs",
      "steps": [
        "kampa (“comb”) is supplied as context.",
        "mp → mm gives the weak stem kamma-.",
        "Add plural -t: kammat (“combs”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "takki → takit",
      "english": "coat → coats",
      "steps": [
        "takki (“coat”) is supplied as context.",
        "kk → k gives the weak stem taki-.",
        "Add plural -t: takit (“coats”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "katto → katot",
      "english": "roof → roofs",
      "steps": [
        "katto (“roof”) is supplied as context.",
        "tt → t gives the weak stem kato-.",
        "Add plural -t: katot (“roofs”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "tyttö → tytöt",
      "english": "girl → girls",
      "steps": [
        "tyttö (“girl”) is supplied as context.",
        "tt → t gives the weak stem tytö-.",
        "Add plural -t: tytöt (“girls”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "ranta → rannat",
      "english": "beach → beaches",
      "steps": [
        "ranta (“beach”) is supplied as context.",
        "nt → nn gives the weak stem ranna-.",
        "Add plural -t: rannat (“beaches”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finnish": "pelto → pellot",
      "english": "field → fields",
      "steps": [
        "pelto (“field”) is supplied as context.",
        "lt → ll gives the weak stem pello-.",
        "Add plural -t: pellot (“fields”)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "Do not attach -t to the unchanged dictionary form when KPT is required.",
    "Do not count the final plural -t as part of the KPT change.",
    "Use the learned stem for that word; spelling cannot always be guessed from English."
  ],
